e but there's  still plenty of room to write the story  of Jimmy McGill transformation into Saul  without rewriting what we already know  Kim and Jimmy were married in May of  2004 so there's still roughly four years  until the two timelines would overlap  one thing worth mentioning about that  flash-forward from quite a ride in  season four is that Jimmy asked  Francesca to be at a phone booth at 3:00  p.m. on  were twelve before they part ways in his  office she agrees to be there to take  this call we know this is Jimmy's  birthday from seeing his driver's  license and that leads people to guess  that Kim would be the most likely caller  who else besides Kim would be planning  to make a call like that one that was  planned well in advance if it is her  then that makes the idea of her still  being together with Jimmy much more  complicated not only would she have to  have been hidden off-screen but she'd  also have to leave him by the time he  uses Edie the vacuum cleaner guy to  disappear while her being the one to  make the phone call would complicate  this outcome it would actually make the  next one impossible that next possible  outcome is that Kim dies it's hard to  imagine this happening and some fans  will tell you that it couldn't happen  but it definitely could there's no  shortage of violence on the cartel side  of this story and for that reason no  character is safe fans love Kim the  creator's love Kim but that doesn't mean  that she can't die Kim has recently made  herself known to the cartel by visiting  Lalo in jail and the fact that Jimmy has  told her about his dealings with them  means she's more than just a family  member that they could use as leverage  to pressure him she knows about their  business and that means she could be a  liability  the only real pros to this outcome is  that Jimmy would be untethered with  nothing holding him back from going full  saw Kim dying would sever all the  remaining ties to that period of time  when Jimmy was trying to be a good guy  trying to do the right thing if we look  at Jimmy after Chuck's death you could  make an argument on how this would clear  his path to where he ends up later Chuck  dying opened the door to Jimmy  practicing law while fully embracing the  conman side of himself after he was  reinstated he changed his name and went  straight to trying to appeal to this  criminal clientele he built up while he  was selling burner phones it's hard to  imagine him doing this if Chuck were  still alive and the other things we saw  what Chuck's death was that Jimmy wasn't  able to process the event he pushed down  his feelings in an unhealthy  Wayne and we just saw them coming back  up when he tore in the Howard outside  the courtroom in Episode seven JMM if  you take him out of the picture  permanently it might be the thing to  push Jimmy over the edge to fully  embracing Saul would it though the cons  of this beyond the fact that killing off  Kim Wexler feels like a crime against  humanity at this point all stem from  that question would he be the guy we met  in Breaking Bad if Kim died he's not a  dark character he's almost  happy-go-lucky  and he definitely seems to enjoy what he  does like he likes being a criminal  lawyer would he be like that if his  early encounters working for criminals  led to the death of someone we can see  that he does truly love there is some  time for healing but to this point Jimmy  doesn't do healing and if he did recover  from the low place he would surely go if  Kim ends up dead would he come out the  other side and jump right back into  criminal law maybe but it would take  some finessing and that's why I favor  the last possible outcome that outcome  is that Kim leaves she's not in the  picture they're not together something  drives these two apart the current  situation with the cartel could be that  thing that finally pushes her to make  the decision to leave Jimmy for good in  that scenario knowing that his decisions  led to Kim becoming the one that got  away could be the thing that completes  his transformation into Saul or Jimmy  fearing for her safety now that Lola  knows about her existence could do  something to drive her away himself a  noble sacrifice to save the woman he  loves even though the price to be paid  would be losing her forever well I like  the idea of her leaving better than the  other two options there are a ton of  potential problems with it as well  primarily the reality of once you're in  you're in  there should be no walking away from the  cartel just because you don't feel like  being involved with them anymore if  you've been on the inside and have  witnessed the workings of the  organization then you're a threat to  bring it down they can't afford to have  loose ends out there in the world which  could put them at risk down the road  after the events a bag man things are  going to be tricky for Jimmy and Kim in  relation to Lalo this has led to the  theory that Jimmy might have to use the  $100,000 he made from picking up the  money to pay heed from the vacuum  cleaner store to help Kim get out of  town while this would answer the  question of how Saul met Ed and knew  about it services while leaving Kim on  the board to be the one who makes the  call Francesca will be waiting for I'm  still not totally in love with this idea  partly because this is something we've  seen happen in the end of so many  characters stories already but also  because I'm not sure it would make sense  that Kim would have to disappear while  Jimmy would be able to just stay and  continue on with his life after the fact  Lalo and the cartel complicate  everything and that's led to the idea  that Kim will figure out some way to  neutralize that threat this is a  promising idea this is an area where  we've seen them shine together in the  past on more than one occasion they work  together well when they have a reason to  and getting out from under Lalo's  influence would be their most impressive  accomplishment to date they could  definitely pull it off and you'd love to  see it but then the question becomes how  does a victory against the cartel turn  into Kim not being around during  Breaking Bad something would have to  happen in this process to drive her away  could doing what becomes necessary to do  be enough to make him decide that she no  longer wants anything to do with Jimmy  McGill it's certainly possible  I should mention because I know I'll get  bombed in the comments that they can't  kill all reason being because Jimmy  fears that he's still alive whenever  Walt and Jesse take him to the desert in  season 2 of Breaking Bad when we first  meet him that doesn't mean that Lalo is  alive it just means that at that point  Jimmy thinks he's alive so they would  have to do something that gets him out  of the picture and for this to fit into  the idea that Kim isn't going to be in  the story any more there would have to  be consequences that come along with it  that would have to make her want to  leave so it is pretty fun that any one  of these could be the possible outcome I  lean towards her leaving not  dying and that would leave things open  for a possible reunion in the gene time  line I'm not a hundred percent on board  with that it's certainly possible he's  in Nebraska we know that Kim grew up in  Nebraska this leads a lot of fans to  thinking for sure that they're going to  at least have an encounter at the end if  not come back together but I'm not a  hundred percent on board with that idea  yet I'm holding out to see what happens  next in the jean story before I decide  if I think that's where they're heading  but in general I do prefer the idea of  her leaving and getting out alive so  tell me in the comments what you think  why do you like whatever idea it is you  think and let's have a conversation  there for what it's worth I don't think  that she'll leave by the end of season  five if that's the way they go I think  that'll happen later if they kill her  off in a shocking way that could happen  at the end of season five but you also  wonder because Rhea seehorn is so great  and this character has carried a lot of  Jimi's story how would they go about not  having her in season six so I'll leave  it there please let me know what you  think about that please like this video  if you enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already thanks  for watching I will talk to you soon
 

